--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
FFmpeg — a deliberate packaging decision
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

  GuitarLab does NOT bundle an FFmpeg binary. It invokes whichever `ffmpeg` and
  `ffprobe` are on your PATH as separate processes (see src/main/media/ffmpeg.ts
  and the FFMPEG_PATH setting).

  This is intentional. Calling a program over its command line does not create a
  derivative work, so FFmpeg's GPL/LGPL terms do not reach this MIT codebase.
  Most prebuilt FFmpeg distributions (gyan.dev, BtbN) are compiled with
  --enable-gpl. Shipping one inside the installer would turn a clean separation
  into a "mere aggregation vs. combined work" argument.

  Do not add an FFmpeg binary to the installer or to this repository.

  Note: dist/win-unpacked/ffmpeg.dll is a different thing entirely — it is
  Chromium's restricted LGPL build, supplied by Electron and covered by
  Electron's own license.
